@startuml auto-renew-stop
title Proxy Auto-Renew: Client Disconnect / Stop Scenarios

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam participantPadding 20
skinparam boxPadding 10
skinparam noteFontSize 11

actor "v5 Client" as Client
box "Proxy" #LightBlue
    participant "ReceiveMessage\nActivity" as RMA
    participant "DefaultReceipt\nHandleManager" as DRHM
    participant "ReceiptHandle\nProcessor\n(eventListener)" as RHP
    participant "ScheduledThread\n(every 5s)" as Sched
end box
participant "ChangeInvisible\nTimeProcessor\n(Broker)" as CIT
participant "PopRevive\nService\n(Broker)" as Revive

== Setup: client receives message ==

Client -> RMA : ReceiveMessage(autoRenew=true)
RMA -> RMA : autoRenew = enableProxyAutoRenew && request.getAutoRenew()
RMA -> DRHM : addReceiptHandle(channel, group, msgID, MessageReceiptHandle)\n[consumeTimestamp=popTime, renewTimes=0, renewRetryTimes=0]
RMA --> Client : message + receiptHandle

note over DRHM
  ReceiptHandleGroup keyed by (channel, group)
  Each handle tracks:
    consumeTimestamp  = popTime  ← immutable
    renewTimes        = 0
    renewRetryTimes   = 0
end note

== Normal auto-renew loop ==

loop every 5s until stopped
    Sched -> DRHM : scheduleRenewTask()
    DRHM -> DRHM : for each (key, group): clientIsOffline? → skip/clear\nfor each handle: nextVisibleTime - now <= 10s?
    DRHM -> DRHM : renewalWorkerService.submit(renewMessage)
    DRHM -> RHP : fireEvent(RENEW, renewTime=RenewStrategyPolicy[renewTimes])\n[0→1m, 1→3m, 2→5m, 3→10m, 4→30m, 5+→1h]
    RHP -> CIT : changeInvisibleTime(handle, invisibleTime=renewTime)
    CIT -> CIT : write new CK (reviveTime=now+renewTime)\nACK old CK
    CIT --> RHP : AckResult.OK
    RHP --> DRHM : updateReceiptHandle(newHandle)\nresetRenewRetryTimes()\nrenewTimes++
end

== Scenario B1: Client channel closes ==

Client ->x RMA : [TCP disconnect / gRPC stream closed]
note right of Client
  Netty fires channelInactive
  → ConsumerManager removes channel
  → ConsumerGroupEvent.CLIENT_UNREGISTER
end note

RMA -> DRHM : CLIENT_UNREGISTER event\n(ConsumerIdsChangeListener)
DRHM -> DRHM : clearGroup(ReceiptHandleGroupKey(channel, group))\n→ receiptHandleGroupMap.remove(key)\n→ returnHandleGroupWorkerService.submit(returnHandleGroup)

loop for each handle in group
    DRHM -> RHP : fireEvent(CLEAR_GROUP, renewTime=1000ms)
    RHP -> CIT : changeInvisibleTime(handle, invisibleTime=1s)
    CIT -> CIT : write new CK (reviveTime=now+1s)\nACK old CK
    CIT --> RHP : AckResult.OK
    RHP --> DRHM : handleData.needRemove=true → evicted
end

note over DRHM
  Fallback: if handle was locked during clearGroup,
  group put back into map.
  Next scheduleRenewTask (≤5s) detects clientIsOffline()
  → clearGroup() again → same 1s CLEAR_GROUP path
end note

CIT -> Revive : [~1s later] CK.reviveTime expires
Revive -> Revive : mergeAndRevive() → reviveRetry()\n→ put to %RETRY%group (reconsumeTimes+1)

== Scenario B2: renewMaxTimeMillis exceeded (3h) ==

note over Sched
  Client still alive, but
  now - consumeTimestamp >= 3h
  (default renewMaxTimeMillis)
end note

Sched -> DRHM : scheduleRenewTask() → renewMessage()
DRHM -> DRHM : startRenewMessage():\n  current - consumeTimestamp >= 3h → STOP_RENEW

DRHM -> DRHM : retryPolicy = subscriptionGroupConfig\n             .getGroupRetryPolicy().getRetryPolicy()\n  delay = retryPolicy.nextDelayDuration(reconsumeTimes)
DRHM -> RHP : fireEvent(STOP_RENEW, renewTime=retryDelay)
RHP -> CIT : changeInvisibleTime(handle, invisibleTime=retryDelay)
CIT -> CIT : write new CK (reviveTime=now+retryDelay)\nACK old CK
CIT --> RHP : AckResult.OK
RHP --> DRHM : resFuture.complete(null) → handle evicted

note right of DRHM
  Proxy no longer tracks this message.
  reconsumeTimes unchanged here —
  broker increments it when reviveRetry fires.
end note

CIT -> Revive : [after retryDelay] CK expires
Revive -> Revive : reviveRetry() → %RETRY%group\n(reconsumeTimes+1)

== Scenario B3: Renew RPC repeatedly fails ==

Sched -> DRHM : scheduleRenewTask() → renewMessage()
DRHM -> RHP : fireEvent(RENEW, ...)
RHP -> CIT : changeInvisibleTime(handle, ...)
CIT --x RHP : [network error / broker unavailable]
RHP --> DRHM : onFailure → renewRetryTimes++\nresFuture.complete(messageReceiptHandle) ← keep in map

note over DRHM
  Retried on next scheduleRenewTask tick (5s).
  After renewRetryTimes >= maxRenewRetryTimes (3):
    return completedFuture(null) → handle evicted
    NO changeInvisibleTime sent
end note

DRHM -> DRHM : renewRetryTimes >= 3:\n  return null → handle evicted\n  (no NACK sent to broker)

CIT -> Revive : [original CK reviveTime expires naturally]
Revive -> Revive : reviveRetry() → %RETRY%group\n(reconsumeTimes+1)

== Outcome comparison ==

note over Client, Revive
  | Scenario                  | renewTime sent    | Handle evicted | Re-appears after       |
  |---------------------------|-------------------|----------------|------------------------|
  | B1: Client disconnect     | 1000ms            | Immediately    | ~1s                    |
  | B1: Detected via scheduler| 1000ms            | ≤5s+1s         | ≤7s                    |
  | B2: renewMaxTimeMillis 3h | retryPolicy delay | Immediately    | retry delay seconds    |
  | B3: Max renew retries (3) | (nothing sent)    | Immediately    | original CK expiry     |
end note

@enduml
